{"base_rate":0.522189349112426,"brier":0.3017266272189349,"bss":-0.2092881642533262,"bss_hi":-0.06654065358376689,"bss_lo":-0.35590199700415287,"chart":{"base":[513.4,305.1],"fp":[138.6,76.9],"lead":"62,269.3 272,264.2 482,261.7 692,235.9","note":{"base":"skill -0.21 — higher than 5% of cities","fp":"low end -5pp, high end +34pp","lead":"day-1 error 0.9 °C — better than 79% of cities","rel":"promised 32% → rained 14%; promised 100% → rained 76%"},"rel":"260.7,403.8 589.8,285.2 667.6,250 691.6,139.3"},"country":"GA","deep":false,"depth":["Rain-probability calibration","Calibration curve","Seasonal split"],"ece":0.30535502958579885,"ess":319.107438872773,"html":{"answer":"\n<h2 id=\"answer\">The short answer for Libreville</h2>\n<div class=\"verdict\">\n<p class=\"lead\"><b>The Libreville rain forecast is cannot beat its own climatology, though 6 points on its probability scale are off by more than chance explains.</b></p>\n<p>When it says rain is <i>near certain</i> (100%), believe about\n<b>76%</b>. When it says rain is <i>very unlikely</i>\n(14%), there is still roughly a <b>6%</b> chance.</p>\n<p class=\"muted\">Based on 676 days, 2024-04-26 to\n2026-03-25. \"Rain\" means at least 0.2 mm measured at\nthe station, 8.7 km from the forecast grid point.\nSkill score -0.21, ranked 205 of\n216 &mdash; but see the rank <i>range</i>\n(197&ndash;207) before reading anything into\nthat position.</p>\n</div>\n\n<h3>What the percentages actually mean here</h3>\n<div class=\"tablewrap\">\n<table><thead><tr><th class=\"num\">It said</th><th class=\"num\">It rained</th>\n<th class=\"num\">Days</th><th>Verdict</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td class='num'>14%</td><td class='num'><b>6%</b></td><td class='num'>68</td><td><span class=\"tag good\">honest</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>50%</td><td class='num'><b>23%</b></td><td class='num'>64</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">overpromised</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>78%</td><td class='num'><b>36%</b></td><td class='num'>69</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">overpromised</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>90%</td><td class='num'><b>48%</b></td><td class='num'>60</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">overpromised</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>94%</td><td class='num'><b>59%</b></td><td class='num'>39</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">overpromised</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>97%</td><td class='num'><b>46%</b></td><td class='num'>93</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">overpromised</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>100%</td><td class='num'><b>76%</b></td><td class='num'>283</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">overpromised</span></td></tr></tbody></table>\n</div>\n<p class=\"muted\">6 of 7 groups are further from honest than chance\nalone can explain. The rest are indistinguishable from a perfect forecast.</p>\n","card":"\n<div class=\"gcard\">\n  <p class=\"gcard-head\"><b>Libreville</b> <span class=\"muted\">Gabon</span></p>\n  <div class=\"gcard-tier\"><span class=\"tag bad\">Cannot beat climatology</span><details class=\"ginfo\"><summary aria-label=\"What does this label mean?\" title=\"What does this label mean?\">?</summary><div class=\"ginfo-pop\" role=\"note\"><p>Compared with a simple guess: saying &ldquo;52% chance of rain&rdquo; every day, because it rains here on 52% of days.</p><p>The forecast did worse than that guess.</p><p><a href=\"#bss\">How the skill score works</a></p></div></details>\n    <span class=\"muted\">6 points off by more than chance</span></div>\n  <dl class=\"gcard-stats\">\n    <div><dt>Skill score<details class=\"ginfo\"><summary aria-label=\"What is the skill score?\" title=\"What is the skill score?\">?</summary><div class=\"ginfo-pop\" role=\"note\"><p>How much better the forecast is than that simple guess. 0 means no better, 1 means perfect, below 0 means worse. Day-ahead rain forecasts usually score 0.3 to 0.5.</p><p><a href=\"#bss\">How the skill score works</a></p></div></details></dt><dd>-0.21</dd></div>\n    <div><dt>Rank</dt><dd>197&ndash;207\n      <span class=\"muted\">of 216</span></dd></div>\n    <div><dt>Record</dt><dd>676 <span class=\"muted\">days</span></dd></div>\n  </dl>\n  <p class=\"gcard-more\"><a href=\"#answer\">The full verdict for\n    Libreville &darr;</a></p>\n</div>","curve":"\n<h2 id=\"curve\">The calibration curve</h2>\n<p>Each dot is a group of days sharing a similar forecast. Horizontal position\nis what was promised; vertical is what happened. <b>On the dashed diagonal =\nhonest.</b> Hover any dot for its sample size.</p>\n<figure><svg viewBox=\"0 0 430 430\" width=\"100%\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Calibration curve for Libreville\"><rect class=\"chart-plot\" x=\"58\" y=\"18\" width=\"354\" height=\"364\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"58\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"382\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"58\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">0%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"386\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">0%</text><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"146.5\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"146.5\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"291.0\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"291.0\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"146.5\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">25%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"295.0\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">25%</text><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"235.0\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"235.0\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"200.0\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"200.0\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"235.0\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">50%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"204.0\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">50%</text><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"323.5\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"323.5\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"109.0\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"109.0\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"323.5\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">75%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"113.0\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">75%</text><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"412\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"18\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"18\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"412\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">100%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"22\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">100%</text><polygon class=\"chart-band\" points=\"106.51882352941175,301.70588235294116 236.71468750000003,154.5 334.01739130434777,65.47826086956525 378.19300000000004,30.133333333333326 391.4861538461538,18.0 401.1516129032257,18.0 411.7873498233216,18.0 411.7873498233216,19.286219081272066 401.1516129032257,45.39784946236563 391.4861538461538,64.66666666666669 378.19300000000004,84.73333333333335 334.01739130434777,134.05797101449275 236.71468750000003,239.8125 106.51882352941175,360.5882352941176\" opacity=\"0.16\"/><line class=\"chart-ideal\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"18\" stroke-dasharray=\"5,4\" stroke-width=\"1.3\"/><line class=\"chart-base\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"191.92307692307693\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"191.92307692307693\" stroke-dasharray=\"2,3\"/><polyline class=\"chart-line\" points=\"106.51882352941175,360.5882352941176 236.71468750000003,296.6875 334.01739130434777,250.1159420289855 378.19300000000004,206.06666666666666 391.4861538461538,167.33333333333331 401.1516129032257,213.6989247311828 411.7873498233216,106.74911660777383\" fill=\"none\" stroke-width=\"2.4\"/><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 14%&amp;#10;It rained 6% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 68 days&amp;#10;within the range a perfect forecast would give\"><circle class=\"chart-dot\" cx=\"106.51882352941175\" cy=\"360.5882352941176\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 50%&amp;#10;It rained 23% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 64 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"236.71468750000003\" cy=\"296.6875\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 78%&amp;#10;It rained 36% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 69 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"334.01739130434777\" cy=\"250.1159420289855\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 90%&amp;#10;It rained 48% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 60 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"378.19300000000004\" cy=\"206.06666666666666\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 94%&amp;#10;It rained 59% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 39 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"391.4861538461538\" cy=\"167.33333333333331\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 97%&amp;#10;It rained 46% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 93 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"401.1516129032257\" cy=\"213.6989247311828\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 100%&amp;#10;It rained 76% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 283 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"411.7873498233216\" cy=\"106.74911660777383\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><text class=\"chart-label\" x=\"235.0\" y=\"422\" font-size=\"12.5\" text-anchor=\"middle\">What the forecast promised</text><text class=\"chart-label\" x=\"15\" y=\"200.0\" font-size=\"12.5\" text-anchor=\"middle\" transform=\"rotate(-90 15 200.0)\">How often it actually rained</text></svg>\n<figcaption>Green band = where a <b>flawless</b> forecast would still land, given\nhow few days we have. Red dots fall outside it, so those are real errors rather\nthan noise. The faint horizontal line is climatology\n(52%).</figcaption></figure>\n","season":"\n<h2 id=\"season\">Does the season matter?</h2>\n<p>In Libreville the forecast is most skilful in\n<b>autumn</b> (-0.09) and least in\n<b>summer</b> (-1.39).</p>\n<div class=\"tablewrap\">\n<table><thead><tr><th>Season</th><th class=\"num\">Days</th>\n<th class=\"num\">Rain days</th><th class=\"num\">Skill score</th>\n<th class=\"num\">Avg error</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>summer</td><td class='num'>176</td><td class='num'>16%</td><td class='num'>-1.394</td><td class='num'>36.3%</td></tr><tr><td>winter</td><td class='num'>171</td><td class='num'>57%</td><td class='num'>-0.524</td><td class='num'>37.6%</td></tr><tr><td>spring</td><td class='num'>150</td><td class='num'>59%</td><td class='num'>-0.326</td><td class='num'>31.6%</td></tr><tr><td>autumn</td><td class='num'>179</td><td class='num'>78%</td><td class='num'>-0.088</td><td class='num'>17.2%</td></tr></tbody></table>\n</div>\n<p class=\"muted\">Four-way splits of a two-year record are thin, so read the\nordering as indicative. Coarser binning is used here than for the annual curve\nfor the same reason.</p>\n"},"lat":0.39241,"lon":9.45356,"n":676,"n_cities":216,"name":"Libreville","offset_days":0,"pop_map":[{"hi":0.325,"lo":0.0,"mean":0.13705882352941173,"n":68,"obs":0.058823529411764705,"sig":false},{"hi":0.67,"lo":0.325,"mean":0.50484375,"n":64,"obs":0.234375,"sig":true},{"hi":0.88,"lo":0.67,"mean":0.7797101449275361,"n":69,"obs":0.36231884057971014,"sig":true},{"hi":0.94,"lo":0.88,"mean":0.9045000000000001,"n":60,"obs":0.48333333333333334,"sig":true},{"hi":0.96,"lo":0.94,"mean":0.942051282051282,"n":39,"obs":0.5897435897435898,"sig":true},{"hi":0.99,"lo":0.96,"mean":0.9693548387096772,"n":93,"obs":0.46236559139784944,"sig":true},{"hi":1.0,"lo":0.99,"mean":0.9993992932862192,"n":283,"obs":0.7561837455830389,"sig":true}],"prcp_km":8.7,"provisional":false,"rank":205,"rank_hi":207.0,"rank_lo":197.0,"reliability":0.10835436969017784,"resolution":0.05586074128861021,"skill_pct":null,"slug":"l